What you may do
---------------

You may copy and redistribute these images in any medium or format, and
you may remix, transform, and build upon them for any purpose, including
commercially. Reuse in a journal article, a textbook, a course pack, a
conference slide, or a grant application is all permitted.


What you must do
----------------

Give appropriate credit, provide a link to the license, and indicate
whether you made changes. You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not
in any way that suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.


Suggested attribution
---------------------

For an unmodified image:

    "PyMOL Shortcuts Manager" screenshot by Blaine Mooers, University of
    Oklahoma Health Campus, licensed under CC BY 4.0.
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Source: https://github.com/MooersLab/pymolshortcuts-manager

For a cropped, recolored, or otherwise altered image, add a statement of
what changed, for example "cropped to the Shortcuts table".

In a figure legend where space is tight, this short form is adequate:

    Screenshot by B. Mooers, CC BY 4.0.


Scope
-----

This notice covers the original content of the images, which is the
graphical user interface of the PyMOL Shortcuts Manager plugin and the
molecular renderings produced with it. It does not purport to license
third-party trademarks, logos, or interface elements belonging to
Schrodinger, to the Qt Company, or to any operating-system vendor that
may appear incidentally within a screenshot. Atomic coordinates shown in
the renderings come from the Protein Data Bank and carry no copyright.


